WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.800
PEFT.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.081
Parameter-efficient fine-tuning.

3
00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:07.300
LoRA is the star, but it has siblings worth knowing.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.867
PEFT is both an umbrella term and a library.

5
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:18.427
The term covers any method that adapts a model while touching only a small fraction of its parameters.

6
00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:21.067
The library puts them behind one interface.

7
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:25.400
The base model stays frozen, so forgetting is structurally impossible.

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.633
Meet the family.

9
00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:31.118
LoRA adds low rank bypass matrices in attention.

10
00:00:31.118 --> 00:00:34.700
It's the default, with the best quality on most tasks.

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.633
Prompt tuning learns about twenty virtual token embeddings placed before the input.

12
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:45.200
Prefix tuning learns virtual key and value vectors inside every attention layer.

13
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.667
And IA3 learns per channel scaling vectors, with even fewer parameters than LoRA.

14
00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:53.033
Here's the trade-off.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.067
LoRA trains about point two two percent of parameters, and gives the best quality on most tasks.

16
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:03.434
Prompt tuning trains only about point zero zero three percent.

17
00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.533
It's weaker, but absurdly cheap.

18
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.833
The library makes comparison easy.

19
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:12.933
We define two configs, one for LoRA and one for prompt tuning.

20
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:17.367
Then the same call wraps the model with either, and prints how much is trainable.

21
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.100
A great portfolio move.

22
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.000
Run the same small fine-tune twice, LoRA and prompt tuning.

23
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.500
Commit a two row table: trainable parameters, minutes to train, and quality on ten held out logs.

24
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.433
It shows you understand the design space, not just a tutorial.

25
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:36.481
Let's recap.

26
00:01:36.481 --> 00:01:39.800
PEFT adapts a model by touching few parameters.

27
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.367
LoRA is the default.

28
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.167
Prompt tuning, prefix tuning and IA3 are its siblings.

29
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.556
The base stays frozen and adapters stay tiny.

30
00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:50.067
Next up: quantization.
